abstract: >
  Verrell's Law is a proposed, falsifiable retained-state selection framework
  investigating whether persistent changes from earlier interactions influence
  future candidate weighting and selection under matched present conditions.
  Its exponential-tilt selection identity is exact under stated mathematical
  assumptions; empirical distinctiveness remains under investigation. Biological,
  computational and material retained-state processes may provide testable
  implementations. Electromagnetic field memory and quantum-collapse proposals
  belong to separate exploratory physical extensions and are not required.
  This metadata reflects the 4 November 2026 scope clarification; earlier
  descriptions remain in the repository history.

